Subject: [PATCH] k60: retain display layers and recompose damaged footprints

Prepared against XNU8796.141.3 after the current patches/xnu/series.
Targets only iokit/Kernel/MiniIOMobileFramebuffer.cpp; no touch/GPU hardware
initialization, boot identity, framebuffer mode or userland gate changes.

The actual20G81 IOMobileFramebufferSwapEnd input is a layer delta: set/clear
masks, enabled flags and valid source/destination rectangles are authoritative.
Unmentioned layers retain one MiniIOSurface holder until replaced or cleared.
Old and new footprints are recomposed from retained layers in premultiplied
BGRA/RGBA source-over order, with clipping that preserves the original transform.
Only damaged scanout rows are written; cached row/column storage is allocated
at startup, never per frame. The first real frame still releases the console.

Prior art: Pong ios16 7798f1e5f261e7121d01d7e4807ed73512737ded, inherited
MiniIOMobileFramebuffer; HakiOS63fc2b4633bac3af8e57dadab9f5a8d4cb940438,
MiniIOMobileFramebuffer.cpp:677-688,1097-1122 for source extent/destination
bounds; original20G81 IOMFB at0x1af17b8a4/0x1af17b9ec/0x1af17ba14/0x1af17be34
for masks and enabled geometry. Pixel blend follows the published iOS vImage
premultiplied BGRA formula (Alpha.h:401-418). Existing license notices remain.

CPU desktop remains the default. Existing explicitly requested GPU scanout
still accepts only one validated full-screen BGRA layer and never races
quarantined DMA. Unsupported layout/invalid surface errors are preserved.

Verification not run by this worker. Main agent owns patch applicability,
host layer smoke, source builds and device rendering observations.

